This repository is a new, minimal implementation. The original EcologyRSI
project was reviewed as a source of architecture and contract ideas, but its
runtime and frontend code are not bundled into this distribution.

The current Python package has no third-party runtime dependencies. It ships
only dataset catalogue metadata and adapters; Autonomous Greenhouse Challenge
raw data are not redistributed. The generated crop-soil-water data remain
engineering fixtures, not scientific observations or validated model output.

The Ecology Evolution plugin integrates with DeepSeek Harness 0.1.0-rc.6 role
presets, Agent sessions, subagents, Workflow Engine, context compaction, and
provider-usage projections. DSH, DeepSeek, and other names may be trademarks
of their respective owners; this project does not claim endorsement by them.

External datasets, model services, papers, and future optional dependencies
must be reviewed under their own licenses before use or redistribution.

The model-selection, environmental-forcing, calibration/validation, and
coupling guidance used while preparing the design documents is adapted from:

